# Forge Lab — private local repo.
# Rule: version the CODE, the DOCS and the small PLANS. Leave out generated media and
# build output — they are big (runs/ 187M, drafts/ 73M, episodes/ 130M, dist/ 56M) and
# fully regenerable from the code. If a run's media ever needs keeping, copy it somewhere
# deliberate rather than committing it.

# ---- build + interpreter noise ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
dist/
build/
_backups/
*.log
.DS_Store
.venv/

# ---- generated media (by extension, so the PLANS beside it stay versioned) ----
# episodes/ holds long-video plans (plan.json) next to their takes: keep the plans, drop
# the media. Same reasoning for runs/ and drafts/.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.gif
episodes/**/*.png
runs/**/*.png
runs/**/*.json
drafts/**/*.png
drafts/**/*.html
drafts/**/*.jpg

# ---- reference assets uploaded to forge (binary, bulky, re-pickable) ----
inputs/

# ---- local-only state ----
forge_host.txt
forge_lab_errors.log
polish_debug.log
wheel_debug.log
/*.png
episodes/test*/

# ---- characters/: same shape as episodes/ — KEEP character.json (a small plan, worth
# versioning: it is the identity block + seed + LoRA), DROP the still (media, re-pickable).
characters/**/*.png
characters/**/*.jpg
